 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Free time",
     "texto": [
      "**Os tempos livres** is «free time». **O que gostas de fazer nos tempos livres?** = what do you like to do in your free time?",
      "Remember that «gostar» takes **de** also with verbs: gosto **de** ler (I like reading), **de** ouvir música (listening to music), **de** passear (going for walks), **de** viajar (travelling), **de** dançar (dancing).",
      "In English you «play» both sports and instruments, but in Portuguese sports take **jogar** and instruments take **tocar**: jogar futebol (to play football), tocar guitarra (to play the guitar)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "I'm doing: «estar a» + infinitive",
     "texto": [
      "In European Portuguese it is very common to express an action in progress with **estar a + infinitive**: **Estou a ler** = I'm reading. **Está a chover** = it's raining.",
      "**O que estás a fazer?** = what are you doing? The gerund (the -ing form) is also heard in some varieties of Portugal; it is wrong to say it is never used there. In Brazil the gerund is the most usual form."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
